    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.select_last_edges_created - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.select_last_edges_created.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.select_last_edges_created()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function\n    .doc-label .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Select the last N edges that were created.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.select_last_edges_created()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function\n    .doc-label .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Select the last N edges that were created.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.select_last_edges_created()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Select the last N edges that were created.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nSelect the last N edges that were created.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L24557-L24655){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.select_last_edges_created(\n    n,\n    set_op=\"union\",\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Select last edges created](../assets/graphs/select-last-edges-created.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"A six-node grid whose seven edges are labeled 1 to 7 in the order they were created. select_last_edges_created(2) selects the two most recent, D–E and E–F, drawn in the accent color.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nSelects the `n` most recently created edges. The graph keeps\ntrack of the order in which edges were added (see `get_edge_creation_order()`), and this\nmethod takes the tail of that order. Edges that have since been deleted are skipped.\n\nThis is useful in incremental workflows where a step adds a batch of edges and the next\nstep needs to act on just that batch, for example to:\n\n- assign a weight, type, or timestamp to the edges just added with\n  `set_edge_attrs_ws()`\n- roll back the last few additions with `delete_edges_ws()`\n- inspect what a generator or a `fully_connect_nodes_ws()` call produced with\n  `get_edge_df_ws()`\n\nSelection is based on creation order, not on edge IDs. The edges are added to the current\nselection, unless `set_op=` says otherwise, and any node selection is cleared. The\ngraph is modified in place and returned for chaining.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[n]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Number of most recently created edges to select. Must be a non-negative integer (a\n    negative value raises `ValueError`). If `n` is larger than the number of edges,\n    every edge is selected; `n=0` selects nothing.\n\n<code>[set_op]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[&quot;union&quot;]{.st}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   How these edges combine with the current edge selection. `\"union\"` (default) adds them\n    to it, `\"replace\"` makes them the selection, `\"intersect\"` keeps only the selected edges\n    among them, and `\"difference\"` removes them from it.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The same graph (modified in place) for method chaining.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `set_op=` is not `\"union\"`, `\"replace\"`, `\"intersect\"`, or `\"difference\"`.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~select_last_nodes_created`) \n\n:   Select the nodes made last.\n\n[](`~set_edge_attrs_ws`) \n\n:   Set attributes on the selected edges.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nThe edges of this path are made in order, so the last two are `C`-`D` and `D`-`E`:\n\n::: {#52e599dc .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"D\"), (\"D\", \"E\")]\n)\ngraph.select_last_edges_created(2)\n\nsorted(graph.get_selected_edge_ids())\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n[3, 4]\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Payments still pending\n\n`payments()` is a month of payments between 18 accounts at a made-up bank, each directed\nfrom payer to payee. Three payments arrive on the last day of the month and are still\nbeing processed. Selecting the last three edges made marks them as pending, without\ntouching the others:\n\n::: {#85d4dfd8 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\npayments = ec.payments()\n(\n    payments\n    .add_edges([\n        (\"Lena\", \"Ivy\", {\"amount\": 2800, \"date\": \"2026-03-19\"}),\n        (\"Max\", \"Cafe\", {\"amount\": 9, \"date\": \"2026-03-19\"}),\n        (\"Eve\", \"Grocer\", {\"amount\": 71, \"date\": \"2026-03-19\"}),\n    ])\n    .select_last_edges_created(3)\n    .set_edge_attrs_ws(pending=True)\n)\n\npayments.get_edge_df().select(\"amount\", \"date\", \"pending\").tail(4)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```{=html}\n<div><style>\n.dataframe > thead > tr,\n.dataframe > tbody > tr {\n  text-align: right;\n  white-space: pre-wrap;\n}\n</style>\n<small>shape: (4, 3)</small><table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\"><thead><tr><th>amount</th><th>date</th><th>pending</th></tr><tr><td>i64</td><td>str</td><td>bool</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>4850</td><td>&quot;2026-03-18&quot;</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>2800</td><td>&quot;2026-03-19&quot;</td><td>true</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>&quot;2026-03-19&quot;</td><td>true</td></tr><tr><td>71</td><td>&quot;2026-03-19&quot;</td><td>true</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#d066dab1 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\npayments.plot(highlight_edges=\"pending\", label_by=\"label\", seed=3)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quar